  "tables": [
    {
      "caption": "",
      "index": 0,
      "text": "If you would like to practice entering the damped oscillator equation as a custom fit in Graphical Analysis, you can use the sample data set linked below. lightly damped pendulum practice data.txt Download lightly damped pendulum practice data.txt This data set was collected from a lightly damped pendulum, so its amplitude decreases relatively slowly over time. Your experimental setups will likely exhibit stronger damping, meaning the amplitude will decrease more quickly than in this example. Fitting parameters generated: A: 0.1177 ± 0.0006321 B: 0.003679 ± 0.00033 C: 2.988 ± 0.0003761 D: 6.38 ± 0.006466 E: 4.707 ± 0.0002109 RMSE: 0.004892"
    },
    {
      "caption": "",
      "index": 1,
      "text": "A: 0.1177 ± 0.0006321 B: 0.003679 ± 0.00033 C: 2.988 ± 0.0003761 D: 6.38 ± 0.006466 E: 4.707 ± 0.0002109 RMSE: 0.004892"
